# desloppify local state
.desloppify/

# Rust
target/
/rust
/ui-db
.scannerwork
# Rust - Fuzzing
fuzz/target/
fuzz/corpus/
fuzz/artifacts/
coverage/
node_modules/

# Config (contains secrets)
/config.toml

# Frontend
ui/node_modules/
ui/dist/

# pnpm — the content-addressable store lives outside the repo; only a local
# store override would land here. pnpm-lock.yaml and pnpm-workspace.yaml ARE
# tracked.
.pnpm-store/
# The generated TypeScript client stays out of the tree; the OpenAPI spec it is
# generated from (ui/openapi.json) IS tracked, so API changes show up in review
# as a diff of the contract. Refresh it with `task dump-spec`.
ui/src/client/
ui/.env
ui/.env.*.local

# Logs
*.log

# Temp Storage
/tmp/

lcov.info
ui/oxlint-results.sarif
ui/eslint-results.sarif

# Generated SBOMs (task sbom:rust / task security)
/sbom-rust.cdx.json
*.cdx.json
.env

# Local working notes (release trackers, scratch checklists). Kept out of the
# tree so they do not turn up as review surface on a PR.
/todo.md

# Impeccable (design skill, RFC 0003). The skill itself is ~150 vendored files
# that change on every upstream release — install it with `task impeccable:install`
# rather than reviewing it as a diff. `.impeccable/` is per-developer state (live
# mode's port, token and inject journal). PRODUCT.md and DESIGN.md, which are the
# durable design decisions, ARE tracked.
/.claude/skills/impeccable/
/.impeccable/
# ...except the shared detector config. A detector waiver is a design decision
# with a reason attached, and it has to reach CI to mean anything: the rendered
# gate re-runs there, so an ignore that lived only on one machine would fail the
# build for everyone else. One reviewable file; `config.local.json` stays out.
!/.impeccable/
/.impeccable/*
!/.impeccable/config.json
